{"qid":"Q15180","names":["Union of Soviet Socialist Republics"],"title":"Union of Soviet Socialist Republics","endonym":{"native":"Союз Советских Социалистических Республик","lang":"ru"},"capsule":"The USSR, formally constituted in December 1922 by the union of Russia, Ukraine, the Transcaucasian Federation, and Byelorussia, was a single-party socialist state that under Stalin's industrialization drives of the 1930s became a major industrial and military power at enormous human cost, including the famine of 1932–1933 that killed millions in Ukraine and Kazakhstan. After defeating Nazi Germany in 1945 at a cost of approximately 27 million Soviet lives, the USSR established satellite states across Eastern Europe and developed nuclear weapons by 1949, making it one of two Cold War superpowers. Gorbachev's reforms from 1985 unleashed centrifugal national movements; the August 1991 coup attempt accelerated dissolution, and on 25 December 1991 Gorbachev resigned, ending the USSR.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Internal republic boundaries are precisely documented in Soviet administrative records and the 1977 constitution; outer national borders are treaty-defined; high confidence throughout.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Soviet Union","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Soviet-Union"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Soviet Union","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soviet_Union"}],"britannica":"place/Soviet-Union","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Soviet Union","rulers":[{"qid":"Q1394","name":"Vladimir Lenin","nativeName":"Владимир Ильич Ленин","roman":"Vladimir Ilyich Lenin","start":1922,"end":1924,"